# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
38-name_plate_blank.FCMacro

A flat name-plate blank on the lid top, cut SUBTRACTIVELY out of the flutes.

WHAT IT IS
  A rounded rectangle pocketed FluteDepth + NamePlateSink down from the lid's
  top face, so the flute ridges inside it are removed and the area becomes flat
  just below the flute-bottom level. Not a raised pad - Bradley's mockup
  (Body002 "NamePlate") padded UP from the flute bottom to the top face,
  filling the flutes flush. This is the inverse: recessed rather than proud.

GEOMETRY, AND WHERE THE NUMBERS COME FROM

  X - "match up to the bottom of the 2nd flute from each end". The 24 lid
  flutes sit at

      -(Width/2 - FluteMargin) + i * (Width - 2*FluteMargin) / (FluteCountFront - 1)

  so flute 1 is at +/-49.5 and flute 2 at +/-45.1957. The blank's edges land on
  that second flute's CENTRELINE, its deepest line, so the boundary reads as
  deliberate; flute 1 plus the outer half of flute 2 survive as a border each
  side. The floor sits NamePlateSink below that line rather than level with it -
  see below for why it cannot be level.

      NamePlateHalfWidth = Width/2 - FluteMargin
                           - (Width - 2*FluteMargin) / (FluteCountFront - 1)

  Y - 10 mm in from the leading and rear edges of the lid. The plate spans
  y -Depth/2 .. Depth/2 + LidBackThickness (-36 .. 40 today), so:

      front edge = -Depth/2 + NamePlateInset                 = -26
      rear  edge =  Depth/2 + LidBackThickness - NamePlateInset = 30

  Note the plate is NOT symmetric in Y - it overhangs the back by
  LidBackThickness to cap the rear panel - so the two insets are different
  expressions, not one offset from centre.

  Corners keep Bradley's BorderRadius.

WHY THIS SKETCH IS REBUILT RATHER THAN REUSED
  Sketch013 in the mockup dimensions off FOUR external-geometry references
  (GeoIds -3..-6) taken through a SubShapeBinder on Face6. That is exactly the
  dependency behind defect D1 in this model: when the referenced face's edge
  COUNT changes, every external GeoId shifts and the constraints silently point
  at the wrong edges. Macros 02, 08 and 12 stripped that pattern out of every
  other sketch in both documents, and CLAUDE.md records ExternalGeometry as
  empty everywhere. This sketch therefore carries the same shape and the same
  constraint topology, but is dimensioned from the sketch ORIGIN against Params.
  It has no external geometry and no binder.

WHY AT THE TIP OF Body
  Appended after PocketMagnetLid, so it disturbs no existing references, and
  suppressing PocketNamePlate removes the blank cleanly. Same reasoning as the
  flutes (macro 24) and the hinge chamfer (macro 37).

THE MOCKUP IS NOT DELETED
  Body002/Sketch013/Pad005 are saved on disk but were never committed, so
  deleting them could not be undone from git. They are hidden instead. Macro 16
  exports Body and Body001 explicitly, so Body002 does not reach the print
  files either way. Delete it by hand once this is confirmed.

THE FLOOR MUST SIT BELOW THE FLUTE BOTTOMS - NamePlateSink

  First build had the floor at exactly top - FluteDepth, i.e. level with the
  flute bottoms. The blank's X walls run ALONG the flutes and sit exactly on
  the 2nd flute's low line, so the floor was TANGENT to that cylinder down the
  blank's whole length - a zero-dihedral edge.

  MeshPart at LinearDeflection 0.1 reported the plate solid, manifold and free
  of self-intersections. The exported STL did not: Mesh.export's default
  tessellation is ~5x finer (10656 facets where the typed tool wrote 1958) and
  it surfaced exactly ONE self-intersection in 29970 facets, at x = -45.15 -
  the 2nd flute's centreline. A coarse mesh check is not proof.

      NamePlateSink = 0.2   how far the floor sits BELOW the flute bottoms

  0.2 rather than something smaller because the default mesh deviation is
  around 0.1 - a margin under that is smeared away by the tessellation and
  proves nothing. The blank is then FluteDepth + NamePlateSink deep, the flute
  bottoms stand NamePlateSink proud of its floor, and every boundary is a real
  cut instead of a tangency. Visually it is a 0.2 mm deeper recess.

  Same species as macro 37's ChamferWallKeep: a geometry knob that exists
  purely to hold a degenerate case away from zero.

Idempotent: safe to re-run.
"""

import math
import FreeCAD
import Part
import Sketcher
from FreeCAD import Vector, Rotation, Placement

SK = "SketchNamePlate"
PK = "PocketNamePlate"
P = "<<Params>>#VarSet."


def main():
    ld = FreeCAD.getDocument("Lid")
    vs = FreeCAD.getDocument("Params").getObject("VarSet")
    body = ld.getObject("Body")
    log = []

    if "NamePlateInset" not in vs.PropertiesList:
        vs.addProperty("App::PropertyLength", "NamePlateInset", "NamePlate",
                       "Inset of the name-plate blank from the lid's leading and rear "
                       "edges. The X extent is NOT this - it is pinned to the 2nd "
                       "flute's centreline; see macro 38.")
        log.append("added NamePlateInset")
    if "NamePlateInset" not in dict(vs.ExpressionEngine):
        vs.NamePlateInset = 10.0
    if "NamePlateSink" not in vs.PropertiesList:
        vs.addProperty("App::PropertyLength", "NamePlateSink", "NamePlate",
                       "How far the blank's floor sits BELOW the flute bottoms. Must be "
                       "non-zero: at zero the floor is TANGENT to the 2nd flute's cylinder "
                       "along the blank's whole X edge and the exported STL "
                       "self-intersects. See macro 38.")
        log.append("added NamePlateSink")
    if "NamePlateSink" not in dict(vs.ExpressionEngine):
        vs.NamePlateSink = 0.2

    if "BorderRadius" not in vs.PropertiesList:
        vs.addProperty("App::PropertyLength", "BorderRadius", "NamePlate",
                       "Corner radius of the name-plate blank.")
        vs.BorderRadius = 5.0
        log.append("added BorderRadius")
    FreeCAD.getDocument("Params").recompute()

    W = float(vs.Width.Value)
    FM = float(vs.FluteMargin.Value)
    N = int(vs.FluteCountFront)
    D2 = float(vs.Depth.Value) / 2.0
    LBT = float(vs.LidBackThickness.Value)
    INS = float(vs.NamePlateInset.Value)
    R = float(vs.BorderRadius.Value)

    X2 = W / 2.0 - FM - (W - 2.0 * FM) / (N - 1)      # 2nd flute centreline
    YF = -D2 + INS                                     # leading edge inset
    YR = D2 + LBT - INS                                # rear edge inset

    EX_X2 = (P + "Width / 2 - " + P + "FluteMargin - (" + P + "Width - 2 * "
             + P + "FluteMargin) / (" + P + "FluteCountFront - 1)")
    EX_YF = "-" + P + "Depth / 2 + " + P + "NamePlateInset"
    EX_YR = P + "Depth / 2 + " + P + "LidBackThickness - " + P + "NamePlateInset"

    if ld.getObject(SK) is None:
        sk = ld.addObject("Sketcher::SketchObject", SK)
        sk.Label = "NamePlateBlank"
        body.addObject(sk)
        sk.AttachmentSupport = [(ld.getObject("DatumPlane"), "")]
        sk.MapMode = "FlatFace"
        sk.AttachmentOffset = Placement(Vector(0, 0, float(vs.LidTopThickness.Value)),
                                        Rotation(0, 0, 0))
        sk.setExpression(".AttachmentOffset.Base.z", P + "LidTopThickness")

        n = Vector(0, 0, 1)
        # loop: line0(left) arc5 line1(front) arc6 line2(right) arc7 line3(rear) arc4
        sk.addGeometry(Part.LineSegment(Vector(-X2, YR - R, 0), Vector(-X2, YF + R, 0)), False)   # 0
        sk.addGeometry(Part.LineSegment(Vector(-X2 + R, YF, 0), Vector(X2 - R, YF, 0)), False)   # 1
        sk.addGeometry(Part.LineSegment(Vector(X2, YF + R, 0), Vector(X2, YR - R, 0)), False)    # 2
        sk.addGeometry(Part.LineSegment(Vector(X2 - R, YR, 0), Vector(-X2 + R, YR, 0)), False)   # 3
        sk.addGeometry(Part.ArcOfCircle(Part.Circle(Vector(-X2 + R, YR - R, 0), n, R),
                                        math.pi / 2, math.pi), False)                            # 4 top-left
        sk.addGeometry(Part.ArcOfCircle(Part.Circle(Vector(-X2 + R, YF + R, 0), n, R),
                                        math.pi, 3 * math.pi / 2), False)                        # 5 bot-left
        sk.addGeometry(Part.ArcOfCircle(Part.Circle(Vector(X2 - R, YF + R, 0), n, R),
                                        3 * math.pi / 2, 2 * math.pi), False)                    # 6 bot-right
        sk.addGeometry(Part.ArcOfCircle(Part.Circle(Vector(X2 - R, YR - R, 0), n, R),
                                        0.0, math.pi / 2), False)                                # 7 top-right
        sk.addGeometry(Part.Point(Vector(-X2, YR, 0)), True)                                     # 8
        sk.addGeometry(Part.Point(Vector(X2, YF, 0)), True)                                      # 9

        C = Sketcher.Constraint
        for a, ap, b, bp in ((0, 1, 4, 2), (0, 2, 5, 1), (1, 1, 5, 2), (1, 2, 6, 1),
                             (2, 1, 6, 2), (2, 2, 7, 1), (3, 1, 7, 2), (3, 2, 4, 1)):
            sk.addConstraint(C("Tangent", a, ap, b, bp))
        sk.addConstraint(C("Vertical", 0))
        sk.addConstraint(C("Vertical", 2))
        sk.addConstraint(C("Horizontal", 1))
        sk.addConstraint(C("Horizontal", 3))
        sk.addConstraint(C("Equal", 4, 5))
        sk.addConstraint(C("Equal", 5, 6))
        sk.addConstraint(C("Equal", 6, 7))
        sk.addConstraint(C("PointOnObject", 8, 1, 0))
        sk.addConstraint(C("PointOnObject", 8, 1, 3))
        sk.addConstraint(C("PointOnObject", 9, 1, 1))
        sk.addConstraint(C("PointOnObject", 9, 1, 2))

        for kind, gid, val, expr in (("DistanceX", 8, -X2, "-(" + EX_X2 + ")"),
                                     ("DistanceY", 8, YR, EX_YR),
                                     ("DistanceX", 9, X2, EX_X2),
                                     ("DistanceY", 9, YF, EX_YF)):
            i = sk.addConstraint(C(kind, -1, 1, gid, 1, val))
            sk.setExpression("Constraints[%d]" % i, expr)
        i = sk.addConstraint(C("Radius", 7, R))
        sk.setExpression("Constraints[%d]" % i, P + "BorderRadius")

        ld.recompute()
        log.append("built %s: %d geo, %d constraints, fully constrained=%s, external=%d"
                   % (SK, len(sk.Geometry), len(sk.Constraints), sk.FullyConstrained,
                      len(sk.ExternalGeometry or [])))
    else:
        sk = ld.getObject(SK)
        log.append("%s already present" % SK)

    if ld.getObject(PK) is None:
        pk = ld.addObject("PartDesign::Pocket", PK)
        pk.Label = "NamePlateBlank001"
        pk.Profile = sk
        pk.Type = 0                                   # Length
        pk.setExpression("Length", P + "FluteDepth + " + P + "NamePlateSink")
        if hasattr(pk, "Midplane"):
            pk.Midplane = False
        pk.SideType = "One side"
        pk.BaseFeature = body.Tip
        body.addObject(pk)
        body.Tip = pk
        log.append("appended %s at the tip of Body" % PK)
    else:
        pk = ld.getObject(PK)
        log.append("%s already present" % PK)

    # Re-assert the driving expression EVERY run, not just on creation. Setting it
    # only inside the create branch made the macro silently non-idempotent: adding
    # NamePlateSink changed nothing on a re-run because the branch was skipped.
    pk.setExpression("Length", P + "FluteDepth + " + P + "NamePlateSink")

    mock = ld.getObject("Body002")
    if mock is not None and mock.Visibility:
        mock.Visibility = False
        log.append("hid the additive mockup Body002 (NOT deleted - never committed)")

    for dn in ("Params", "Lid", "MagicCardBox"):
        FreeCAD.getDocument(dn).recompute()

    # ---------------- verify ----------------
    problems = []
    if not sk.FullyConstrained:
        problems.append("%s is not fully constrained" % SK)
    if sk.ExternalGeometry:
        problems.append("%s picked up external geometry" % SK)
    for o in ld.Objects:
        st = o.State or []
        if "Invalid" in st or "Error" in st:
            problems.append("Lid/%s %s" % (o.Name, list(st)))

    plate = body.Shape
    if not (plate.isValid() and plate.isClosed() and len(plate.Solids) == 1):
        problems.append("lid plate not a single valid closed solid")

    import MeshPart
    m = MeshPart.meshFromShape(Shape=plate, LinearDeflection=0.1,
                               AngularDeflection=0.5, Relative=False)
    log.append("plate mesh: solid=%s nonmanifold=%s selfint=%s"
               % (m.isSolid(), m.hasNonManifolds(), m.hasSelfIntersections()))
    if not m.isSolid():
        problems.append("plate mesh not watertight")
    if m.hasNonManifolds():
        problems.append("plate mesh non-manifold")
    if float(vs.NamePlateSink.Value) <= 0:
        problems.append("NamePlateSink is 0 - the floor would be tangent to flute 2")

    # measure the blank from the solid
    top = float(vs.Height.Value) + float(vs.LidSeatClearance.Value) + float(vs.LidTopThickness.Value)
    want_floor = top - (float(vs.FluteDepth.Value) + float(vs.NamePlateSink.Value))
    e = Part.makeLine(Vector(0, 0, top + 2), Vector(0, 0, top - 5))
    spans = [(s.BoundBox.ZMin, s.BoundBox.ZMax) for s in plate.common(e).Edges]
    floor = max(hi for _, hi in spans) if spans else None
    log.append("blank floor at z = %.4f (want %.4f = top %.3f - FluteDepth - NamePlateSink)"
               % (floor if floor else -1, want_floor, top))
    if floor is None or abs(floor - want_floor) > 1e-4:
        problems.append("blank floor %.4f != %.4f" % (floor if floor else -1, want_floor))

    log.append("blank extent: x +/-%.4f (2nd flute centreline), y %.3f .. %.3f"
               % (X2, YF, YR))
    log.append("RESULT: %s" % ("FAIL -> " + "; ".join(problems) if problems else "all checks pass"))
    print("\n".join(log))
    if problems:
        raise RuntimeError("; ".join(problems))


main()
